---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="ACP compatibility"
  eyebrow="Protocols"
  description="Connect ACP clients to Roder with persistent sessions, model controls, images, and injected MCP tools."
  prev={{ href: "/docs/app-server/", title: "App server" }}
>
  <p>
    Run <code>roder acp</code> to serve ACP v1 over newline-delimited JSON-RPC on
    stdin/stdout. Diagnostics go to stderr. ACP clients share Roder's runtime,
    tools, permissions, and durable thread store. Native integrations can use the
    broader <a href="/docs/app-server/">app-server protocol</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Connect and authenticate</h2>
  <pre><code>{`npm install -g @roderai/roder
roder auth login codex
roder acp`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    Send <code>initialize</code> and use the running binary's advertised capabilities.
    Fresh installations default to Codex; configured providers and models remain in
    use. With Codex selected, clients can request browser sign-in through
    <code>authenticate</code>. Roder owns provider credentials.
  </p>
  <h2>Persistent sessions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Create sessions with <code>session/new</code>; load or resume stored sessions after restarting the host.</li>
    <li><code>session/list</code> returns saved sessions, optional cwd filtering, and an opaque <code>nextCursor</code>. Pass the cursor unchanged, even after an empty filtered page.</li>
    <li><code>session/close</code> releases active resources without deleting persisted history.</li>
    <li>Text, image prompts, resource links, assistant streaming, tool activity, cancellation, and permission requests translate to the native runtime.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Choose a model and permission mode</h2>
  <p>
    New, loaded, and resumed sessions return <code>modes</code> and
    <code>configOptions</code>. Select an advertised <code>provider/model</code>
    value through <code>session/set_config_option</code> with
    <code>configId: "model"</code>. Model and mode changes require an idle session.
    Both persist per thread.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":4,"method":"session/set_mode","params":{"sessionId":"THREAD_ID","modeId":"plan"}}`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    Modes are <code>default</code>, <code>accept_all</code>, <code>plan</code>,
    and <code>bypass</code>. Injected MCP calls still ask for permission in
    <code>accept_all</code>; <code>plan</code> rejects them because their side effects
    are unknown. <code>bypass</code> runs them without an ACP permission request.
    Team restrictions still take precedence.
  </p>
  <h2>Inject MCP tools</h2>
  <p>
    Supply stdio or streamable HTTP servers through <code>mcpServers</code> when
    creating, loading, or resuming a session. Roder discovers their schemas before
    returning the session. Stdio servers run in the session cwd.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"method":"session/new","params":{
  "cwd":"/absolute/project",
  "mcpServers":[
    {"name":"local","command":"example-mcp","args":[],"env":[]},
    {"type":"http","name":"remote","url":"http://127.0.0.1:9000/mcp","headers":[]}
  ]
}}`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    Tools use <code>mcp__SERVER__TOOL</code> names. Keep credentials and server launch
    configuration in the host. Restoring a session requires resupplying servers
    with exactly the saved tool names, descriptions, and schemas; missing or changed
    bindings fail with <code>-32602</code>. Session close and orderly shutdown close
    MCP clients. SSE, MCP resources, and MCP prompts are not exposed by this adapter.
  </p>
  <h2>Images and host instructions</h2>
  <p>
    Image blocks accept base64 PNG, JPEG, WebP, and GIF with matching MIME types.
    The selected provider must support image input. Paseo hosts can set
    <code>_meta._paseo.systemPrompt</code> on new sessions; Roder stores it as
    developer instructions beneath the harness prompt. Resume must omit it or
    supply the same string. Workspace instructions and policy still apply.
  </p>
  <p>
    These features shipped in CLI 0.3.21 and 0.3.25. See the
    <a href="https://github.com/RoderAI/roder/blob/master/docs/roder-acp.md">ACP integration contract</a>
    and <a href="https://github.com/RoderAI/roder/blob/master/docs/openclaw-acp.md">ACPx and OpenClaw setup</a>
    for host-specific configuration. Session deletion, additional workspace roots,
    audio, and embedded resource content remain unsupported.
  </p>

  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Protocol rule.</strong> ACP should translate into the same runtime events,
    tools, sessions, and policy decisions as every other client surface.
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
